---
interface Props {
  email: string;
  analytics: boolean;
  utmSource: string;
  gamePolicies: Array<{ name: string; url: string; page: string }>;
}
const { email, analytics, utmSource, gamePolicies } = Astro.props;
---

<h2>The short version</h2>
<ul>
  <li>This website sets no cookies and runs no advertising or tracking scripts.</li>
  {
    analytics ? (
      <li>We count visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which works without cookies and without identifying you.</li>
    ) : (
      <li>We don’t use any website analytics.</li>
    )
  }
  <li>If you email us, we use your message only to reply to you.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Who is responsible</h2>
<p>
  This policy covers abravastudio.com, the website of Abrava Studio, an independent game studio based in Serbia. For
  any privacy question, write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>.
</p>

<h2>When you visit the website</h2>
<p>
  The website is hosted and delivered by Cloudflare. To serve pages and protect the site against abuse, Cloudflare
  processes technical data such as your IP address, browser type and the page you requested. Cloudflare acts as our
  service provider; see the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.
</p>

{
  analytics && (
    <>
      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to see which pages are visited, how fast they load, and roughly where visitors
        come from (country and referring website). It does not use cookies or local storage and does not build a profile
        of you. We only see aggregated totals.
      </p>
    </>
  )
}

<h2>Embedded videos</h2>
<p>
  Game pages can show a YouTube video. Nothing is loaded from YouTube until you press play. When you do, the video
  loads from youtube-nocookie.com and the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google privacy policy</a>
  applies.
</p>

<h2>Links to other services</h2>
<p>
  Store buttons and community links take you to Google Play, Discord and YouTube, which have their own privacy
  policies. Links to Google Play carry a campaign tag (<code>utm_source={utmSource}</code>) so we can see, as an
  aggregate number in the Google Play Console, how many players found a game through this website.
</p>

<h2>Email</h2>
<p>
  When you write to <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>, we receive your email address and whatever you include in
  your message. We use it only to answer you, and we keep the conversation only as long as we need it to handle your
  request. We never add you to a mailing list.
</p>

{
  gamePolicies.length > 0 && (
    <>
      <h2>Our games</h2>
      <p>Each of our games has its own privacy policy, which is also linked from its store listing:</p>
      <ul>
        {gamePolicies.map((game) => (
          <li>
            <a href={game.url} rel="noopener">
              {game.name} privacy policy
            </a>{' '}
            (<a href={game.page}>game page</a>)
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </>
  )
}

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>
  You can ask us which personal data we hold about you and ask us to correct or delete it by writing to
  <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. You can also contact your local data protection authority. In Serbia, that is
  the Commissioner for Information of Public Importance and Personal Data Protection.
</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If the way this website handles data changes, we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>
